course: dictionary
lesson: 8983
title: One word, many meanings: sit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sit is a short word with lots of jobs. Most of the time it means to rest your body on a seat or the ground, with your weight on your bottom. The words around it show which meaning is in use. «The potoo sits still on a branch» is about a bird staying in one place, not about a bottom on a seat.
explain: Read the words next to sit. «Sit down», «sit up» and «sit next to» are about your body on a seat. «Sit a test» is different: the word test tells you it means to take one. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Sit changes its form: sits, sat and sitting. «His dad plays a fighting game with him on Sunday mornings, sitting right next to him.» Sitting shows the action going on now, and the words next to him show where.
fact: Sit is a verb, and its forms are sit, sits, sat and sitting.
fact: «Sit down» means rest your body on a seat.
fact: «Sit still» means stay in one place without moving.
fact: «Sit a test» means take a test, and this meaning is used in the UK.
fact: To sit for a dog means to put its bottom down when told.
exercise: «The box sat in the hall for a week.» What does sat mean here? | *Was in a place without moving | Put its bottom down when told | Rested its bottom on a seat | Took a test
exercise: Ella says, «I will sit my maths exam on Monday.» What does sit mean? | To rest on a chair | To stay still on a branch | To put her bottom down when told | *To take the exam
exercise: «He sat down at the table.» Which form of sit is used here? | *sat | sit | sitting | sits
test: «The potoo sits still on a branch looking like a dead stump.» Sits means | Takes an exam | Rests on a seat and stands up | Puts its bottom down when told | *Stays in one place without moving
test: Which word is the past form of sit? | sit | sitting | *sat | sits
exam: Which sentence uses sit to mean take an exam? | «Sit still and listen, please.» | «The dog will sit when you say so.» | *«Jamal will sit his spelling test in June.» | «The box sat in the hall for a week.»
